      en: "The Basilica of San Vitale in Ravenna is an early Christian church from the 6th century. Consecrated in 547, it is famous for its Byzantine mosaics. The basilica has an octagonal plan. The dome mosaics depict Christ. The apse mosaics show Emperor Justinian and Theodora. Built on an earlier structure. Part of the UNESCO World Heritage of early Christian monuments in Ravenna. The interior is adorned with marble and mosaics. Architecture blends Western and Eastern influences.",
