      en: "The Ducal Palace of Urbino is a Renaissance palace built from 1444 for Federico da Montefeltro. Designed by Luciano Laurana and Francesco di Giorgio Martini. It houses the Galleria Nazionale delle Marche with works by Raphael and Piero della Francesca. The architecture exemplifies harmonious proportions. The famous Studiolo is adorned with wood intarsia. The inner courtyard is elegant. The palace dominates the city. The facade features towers and crenellations. UNESCO World Heritage. Construction took about 40 years.",
